{#-
  The video template (SPEC §7.5, §9, §12; project lead, 2026-11-09: "a
  consistent template that is reproduced exactly, without variation"). Every
  video on the site is this macro and nothing else: the problem's own video,
  each open solution card (main and extra) and each Start here chapter. Same
  markup, same CSS (components.css, "Video template"), so they can't drift.
  A build test (video-template.test.js) checks every video on every page.

    {% from "partials/video-block.njk" import videoBlock %}
    {{ videoBlock(video, heading=2, ratings=ratingsOn, feedback=feedbackOn) }}
    {{ videoBlock(video, heading=3, label={ num: 1, text: 'Main' },
                  close=id + '-panel', bleed='card', ratings=ratingsOn,
                  feedback=feedbackOn) }}

  In this order, every time:
    0. the label, if the context has one: a step chip ("1 Main", "2 Extra"
       on a solution card; "1 of 2" on Start here). The problem's own video
       has none. A solution card's Close sits at the label's right.
    1. the title, a heading (h2 on the problem page and Start here, h3 in a
       solution card, under its section's h2), id video-<video_id>-title;
    2. the description. Both are the video's own, from its row of
       data/videos.csv, and so the same wherever the video is: no page can
       give a video another title or description (project lead,
       2026-11-14; SPEC §7.2);
    then the video (partials/video.njk), then one row of controls:
    3. "Audio only": a native <details> holding <audio controls
       preload="none"> (the video's own soundtrack, SPEC §9.2). First, so
       opening it never moves its own button: open, it takes the row's
       full width, the player opens under its button, and the handout,
       "Feedback" and the stars move down under the player;
    4. "Handout": a link to media/pdf/ (the video's text alternative,
       carrying its full narration, SPEC §9.3). The format is still open
       (SPEC §21), so the label is "Handout" and "(PDF)" is said only to
       screen readers. It is the only handout link near the video;
    5. "Feedback" (project lead, 2026-11-13; SPEC §13), while `feedback` is
       exactly true (the callers pass site.features.feedback === true): a
       button that opens the feedback dialog (partials/feedback-dialog.njk,
       which base.njk renders on the same condition) about this video. It
       looks like "Handout", and ships `hidden`, since it needs JavaScript:
       src/js/feedback.js shows it once it opens the dialog, and sends
       data-feedback-video, the video_id, with the message;
    6. "Was this helpful?" and the five stars (partials/rating.njk), while
       `ratings` is exactly true (the callers pass
       site.features.ratings === true); its status line takes a line of
       its own under the row.
  Every row of data/videos.csv names an audio file and a handout (the
  content check fails the build otherwise, SPEC §7.1), so both always render.

  Layout (components.css): decided by the width of the page's two-column
  wrapper (.with-sidebar, the one query container for every video on the
  site, so every video switches at one window width, and the problem video
  and an open card switch together). From 1080px (a 768px main column
  beside a problem page's sidebar: the Problem-A open card's 420 + 24 +
  280 = 724, plus an open card's border and padding) the video (3fr) and
  the label, title and description (2fr) sit side by side and the row runs
  under both; narrower, the label, title and description come first (the
  DOM order), then the video and the row. Every caller must render inside
  .with-sidebar__main, the wrapper's main column.

  Arguments (keyword arguments, all optional after `video`):
    video        a video from `videoById` (or `introChapters`/`solutionsByTier`)
    heading      the title's heading level: 2 (default) or 3
    label        { num, text }: the step chip; none by default
    close        the id of the solution card's panel: adds "Close" at the
                 label's right, ships the header `hidden` and makes the
                 title focusable (tabindex="-1"). Without JavaScript the
                 card's <summary> names it and is its only close control
                 (a button can't close a <details>), so src/js/solutions.js
                 shows the header once Close works, and moves focus to the
                 title when the card opens.
    bleed        'page' (default) or 'card': how the frame meets the edges
                 below 600px (partials/video.njk)
    ratings      exactly true: the ratings widget ends the row
    feedback     exactly true: "Feedback" follows the handout

  Without JavaScript the handout and audio work as they are. src/js/players.js
  pauses other media when audio plays and has the event hooks (data-handout
  and the audio's data-media hold the video_id, whatever the handout's
  format or the audio's file name; SPEC §9.4, §10.2). pages.json reads the
  same attributes, and data-feedback-video (SPEC §8.3), so the Worker accepts
  exactly these ids.

  ids: video-<video_id>-title, audio-<video_id>, and the widget's
  rating-<video_id>-*. The validator allows each video once per page, so
  they are unique.
-#}
{%- from "partials/icons.njk" import icon -%}
{%- from "partials/rating.njk" import rating -%}
{%- from "partials/step-chip.njk" import stepChip -%}
{%- from "partials/video.njk" import videoEmbed -%}
{%- macro videoBlock(video, heading=2, label=none, close='', bleed='page', ratings=false, feedback=false) -%}
{%- set h = 'h3' if heading == 3 else 'h2' -%}
{%- set id = video.video_id -%}
<div class="video-block">
  <div class="video-block__grid">
    <div class="video-block__header"{% if close %} hidden{% endif %}>
      {%- if label or close %}
      <div class="video-block__top">
        {%- if label %}
        {{ stepChip(label.num, label.text) }}
        {%- endif %}
        {%- if close %}
        <button type="button" class="video-block__close" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="{{ close }}">Close<span class="visually-hidden"> {{ video.title }}</span></button>
        {%- endif %}
      </div>
      {%- endif %}
      <{{ h }} class="video-block__title" id="video-{{ id }}-title"{% if close %} tabindex="-1"{% endif %}>{{ video.title }}</{{ h }}>
      <p class="video-block__desc">{{ video.description }}</p>
    </div>
    <div class="video-block__video">
      {{ videoEmbed(video, bleed=bleed) }}
    </div>
    <div class="video-controls">
      <details class="format-disclosure" id="audio-{{ id }}">
        <summary class="format-disclosure__toggle"><span class="format-button">{{ icon('headphones', 18, 'format-button__icon') }}Audio only<span class="visually-hidden">: {{ video.title }}</span>{{ icon('chevron-down', 16, 'format-disclosure__chevron') }}</span></summary>
        <div class="format-disclosure__panel">
          <audio class="format-audio" controls preload="none" src="/media/audio/{{ video.audio }}" data-media="{{ id }}" aria-label="Audio only: {{ video.title }}"><a href="/media/audio/{{ video.audio }}">Download the audio (MP3)</a></audio>
        </div>
      </details>
      <a class="format-button" href="/media/pdf/{{ video.handout }}" type="application/pdf" data-handout="{{ id }}">{{ icon('download', 18, 'format-button__icon') }}Handout<span class="visually-hidden">: {{ video.title }} (PDF)</span></a>
      {%- if feedback === true %}
      <button type="button" class="format-button" data-feedback-trigger data-feedback-video="{{ id }}" hidden>{{ icon('message', 18, 'format-button__icon') }}Feedback<span class="visually-hidden">: {{ video.title }}</span></button>
      {%- endif %}
      {%- if ratings === true %}
      {{ rating(video) }}
      {%- endif %}
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
{%- endmacro -%}
